<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Emirate of Dhala</h1><p class="st-meta">1750 CE – 1967 CE (approx.) · capital Al Dhala</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Amiri emirate on the highland frontier north of Aden, where the armed revolt against British rule in South Arabia began.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Amiri family ruled the district of Dhala, a high plateau on the route between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> and the Yemeni highlands. They became independent of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qasimid-state">Qasimid State</a> in the 18th century. The Zaydi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imams</a> and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> continued to claim the area.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The emir governed through tribal sheikhs and taxed the trade crossing the frontier. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> brought Dhala into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aden-protectorate">Aden Protectorate</a>, and the Anglo-Ottoman boundary of 1904 left it on the British side. British political officers and troops were stationed there, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> was a founding member of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-arab-emirates-of-the-south">Federation of Arab Emirates of the South</a> in 1959.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1963 tribesmen of the nearby Radfan mountains launched the armed struggle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> against the federation. When the NLF took over in 1967 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> was abolished and incorporated into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/emirate-of-dhala.jpg" alt="Emirate of Dhala" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Orange Tuesday (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Dhala.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1750 CE – 1967 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Al Dhala</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Amiri Emirate, Dhala, Ad Dali</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1858&amp;focus=emirate-of-dhala" aria-label="Emirate of Dhala on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5906 1668 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Emirate of Dhala lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6226 1924L6295 1853M6226 1924L6313 1863M6226 1924L6313 1863M6226 1924L6236 1957"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6295 1853h0M6313 1863h0M6313 1863h0M6236 1957h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6226 1924h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6226 1924h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1858&amp;focus=emirate-of-dhala">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
